  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study on seeds and gender equity in Kenya (research for World Bank Gender report)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BIBA-Kenya, a member of our partner AFSA, will conduct research to provide in-depth evidence of the impact of Kenya&#x2019;s seed laws on women as seed savers and farmers. It will demonstrate how the expansion of commercial seed markets, the promotion of hybrid seeds and the undermining of farmer-managed seed systems disproportionately affects women farmers, and women&#x2019;s interests. It will explain the different dimensions of that impact e.g. livelihood, food security, autonomy, social position. It will demonstrate how these impacts affect gender equity and community resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
